    "content": "{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    float *heap_dist = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\\n    char *heap_label = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\\n    int hsize = 0;\\n    float maxd = 0.0f;\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        Group g = groups[i];\\n        float px = to_evaluate.x;\\n        float py = to_evaluate.y;\\n\\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\\n            float dx = g.points[j].x - px;\\n            float dy = g.points[j].y - py;\\n\\n            if (hsize < k) {\\n                float d = dx * dx + dy * dy;\\n                int pos = hsize++;\\n                heap_dist[pos] = d;\\n                heap_label[pos] = g.label;\\n\\n                while (pos > 0) {\\n                    int parent = (pos - 1) >> 1;\\n                    if (heap_dist[parent] < heap_dist[pos]) {\\n                        float td = heap_dist[parent];\\n                        heap_dist[parent] = heap_dist[pos];\\n                        heap_dist[pos] = td;\\n\\n                        char tl = heap_label[parent];\\n                        heap_label[parent] = heap_label[pos];\\n                        heap_label[pos] = tl;\\n\\n                        pos = parent;\\n                    } else {\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n\\n                if (hsize == k) {\\n                    maxd = heap_dist[0];\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                float dx2 = dx * dx;\\n                if (dx2 >= maxd) {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n\\n                float d = dx2 + dy * dy;\\n                if (d < maxd) {\\n                    heap_dist[0] = d;\\n                    heap_label[0] = g.label;\\n\\n                    int pos = 0;\\n                    while (1) {\\n                        int left = (pos << 1) + 1;\\n                        int right = left + 1;\\n                        int largest = pos;\\n\\n                        if (left < hsize && heap_dist[left] > heap_dist[largest]) {\\n                            largest = left;\\n                        }\\n                        if (right < hsize && heap_dist[right] > heap_dist[largest]) {\\n                            largest = right;\\n                        }\\n\\n                        if (largest != pos) {\\n                            float td = heap_dist[pos];\\n                            heap_dist[pos] = heap_dist[largest];\\n                            heap_dist[largest] = td;\\n\\n                            char tl = heap_label[pos];\\n                            heap_label[pos] = heap_label[largest];\\n                            heap_label[largest] = tl;\\n\\n                            pos = largest;\\n                        } else {\\n                            break;\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n\\n                    maxd = heap_dist[0];\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    int freq[256] = {0};\\n    for (int i = 0; i < hsize; i++) {\\n        freq[(unsigned char)heap_label[i]]++;\\n    }\\n\\n    // The original implementation initializes all k slots with label -1.\\n    // If fewer than k points were seen, those missing slots still participate\\n    // in the frequency count and tie-breaking.\\n    if (hsize < k) {\\n        freq[255] += k - hsize;\\n    }\\n\\n    char best = 0;\\n    int best_count = -1;\\n    for (int c = -128; c <= 127; c++) {\\n        unsigned char idx = (unsigned char)c;\\n        if (freq[idx] > best_count) {\\n            best_count = freq[idx];\\n            best = (char)c;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    free(heap_dist);\\n    free(heap_label);\\n    return best;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n    \\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/knn.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Once the max-heap is full, most points are rejected because their squared distance already exceeds the current k-th largest distance. Since d = dx^2 + dy^2 >= dx^2 in floating point for finite inputs, checking only the x-component first avoids computing and adding the y-component for clearly non-qualifying points. Keeping the current heap maximum in a local register also removes repeated root loads from memory while preserving sequential AoS traversal of each group's points for spatial locality.\",\"notes\":\"The early rejection is safe: if dx^2 >= maxd then d >= maxd, so no point that would replace the heap root is skipped. The strict '<' replacement condition and all tie-breaking behavior are unchanged; the local maxd is refreshed after every insertion/replacement that changes the heap root. Only src/knn.c was modified; knn.h remains untouched.\",\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Early x-component squared-distance rejection before computing y-component when heap is full\",\"Cache current k-th largest distance in a local variable and update it after heap modifications\"]}",
